  "report": "ROOT_CAUSE_DIMENSIONS: SITE_NUM, TEMP_C\n\nROOT_CAUSE_VALUES: SITE_NUM=7,3; TEMP_C=25\n\nROOT_CAUSE_STRUCTURE: independent\n\nROOT_CAUSE_EVIDENCE: measured\n\nFINDINGS\n\n1. Overall yield is 95.79% with a measurement failure rate of 0.144% across 112,500 rows and 3,750 parts (get_overall_yield). Top failing tests are vmin_sram and vmin_core, each at 0.178% failure rate (get_failures_by_test).\n\n2. Test site 7 shows 94.0% part yield (worst overall) with 0.207% measurement failure rate across all conditions, and site 3 shows 94.32% yield with 0.189% failure rate, while best performers (sites 5, 8) exceed 96.84% yield (get_yield_summary by SITE_NUM).\n\n3. Room temperature testing (TEMP_C=25) shows elevated failure rate of 0.171% compared to cold (0\u00b0C: 0.107%) and hot (85\u00b0C: 0.155%) across all sites (get_fail_rate_by_condition).\n\n4. At TEMP_C=25, site 3 shows 0.295% failure rate (97.05% yield) and site 7 shows 0.289% failure rate (97.11% yield), while other sites at room temperature range from 0.084% to 0.147% (get_yield_summary by SITE_NUM with TEMP_C=25 filter).\n\n5. For vmin_core test at site 7 and TEMP_C=25, failure rate reaches 0.444%, and at site 3 reaches 0.842%, compared to best-performing sites (1, 5, 8) at 0% failure rate at room temperature (get_fail_rate_by_condition for vmin_core by SITE_NUM).\n\n6. Sites 7 and 3 combined at TEMP_C=25 account for 27 of 63 total failures at room temperature (42.9%), concentrated in vmin_core (6 fails), sram_bist (4 fails), and thermal_diode/io_leakage/idd_static (3 fails each), while all other sites show minimal room-temperature failures (get_failures_by_test with SITE_NUM and TEMP_C filters).\n\n7. Distribution statistics for vmin_sram and vmin_core show similar means and standard deviations across all five wafers, with margin_sigma near 3.0 for both tests, indicating the issue is not a wafer-level process shift (get_distribution_stats grouped by WAFER_ID).\n\nRULED OUT\n\n1. Lot-level effect: While L45 shows slightly lower overall yield (95.07%), the pattern persists across all five lots. The correlation with specific sites at room temperature is primary; lot-level yield degradation is secondary (get_yield_summary by LOT_ID).\n\n2. Wafer-level effect: Yield by wafer ranges from 94.4% (W01) to 96.53% (W02), but distribution statistics are consistent across wafers for both failing tests, and the room-temperature site-specific pattern appears across all wafers (get_distribution_stats grouped by WAFER_ID, get_yield_summary by WAFER_ID).\n\n3. Voltage-level effect as primary cause: While VDD=0.85 shows slightly elevated failure rate (0.157%) versus VDD=0.75 (0.133%), the pattern at sites 7 and 3 at room temperature dominates the excursion and is not strictly voltage-dependent (get_fail_rate_by_condition by voltage).\n\n4. Cold/hot temperature extremes: Failures are minimal at both 0\u00b0C (0.107%) and 85\u00b0C (0.155%), indicating the issue is specific to room temperature testing conditions (get_fail_rate_by_condition by temperature).\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nThe data supports a systematic failure pattern tied to two independent dimensions: test site (specifically sites 7 and 3) and test temperature (specifically 25\u00b0C room temperature). At the intersection of these conditions, vmin_core failures spike to 0.649% combined failure rate for sites 7 and 3, compared to 0% for the best-performing sites at the same temperature. This pattern is consistent across all lots and wafers, indicating a site-specific characterization or instrumentation issue at room temperature rather than a process excursion. The failure mechanism appears related to voltage-sensitive tests (vmin_core and vmin_sram are most affected), suggesting potential temperature-dependent measurement bias or calibration drift at sites 7 and 3 during room-temperature testing. I have quantified the combined effect of both dimensions together (sites 7 and 3 at TEMP_C=25 show elevated failure rates measured directly), and the dimensions contribute independently\u2014each site performs poorly at room temperature regardless of other factors.\n\nRECOMMENDED NEXT STEP\n\nInvestigate the test instrumentation and thermal conditioning at test sites 7 and 3 during room-temperature (25\u00b0C) operation. Check for calibration drift, temperature sensor accuracy, or measurement conditioning issues specific to these sites at this condition. Verify that the thermal chamber or ambient environment is achieving and maintaining exactly 25\u00b0C at these sites. This pattern suggests an ongoing systemic condition affecting only sites 7 and 3 at room temperature, likely related to equipment-level thermal or measurement characterization rather than die quality, since the same parts pass at other sites or temperatures.",
